WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.037
Use the attention demo to click a token and inspect which earlier positions are available to it.

00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:12.792
Future positions stay blocked, while the allowed positions receive normalized attention weights.

00:00:12.792 --> 00:00:19.962
The numbers are illustrative, but the masking behavior matches the core idea used in decoder models.

00:00:19.962 --> 00:00:24.872
When you click a later token, it can look backward to more positions.

00:00:24.872 --> 00:00:29.563
When you click an early token, only a small part of the sequence is available.
